WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.698
Hi! Conjunctions are like glue that join two ideas into one sentence. Today we'll learn and, but, or, so and because.

2
00:00:10.848 --> 00:00:15.114
And adds similar ideas: I like apples and oranges.

3
00:00:15.264 --> 00:00:19.530
But joins opposite ideas: The bag is small but heavy.

4
00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:23.202
Or gives a choice: Do you want tea or milk?

5
00:00:23.352 --> 00:00:31.506
So gives a result and because gives a reason: It rained, so we stayed in. We stayed in because it rained.

6
00:00:31.656 --> 00:00:35.586
First read both parts and ask: how are they linked?

7
00:00:35.736 --> 00:00:39.834
Similar ideas take and, opposite ideas take but.

8
00:00:39.984 --> 00:00:46.794
If the reason comes first, use so. If the result comes first and the reason after, use because.

9
00:00:46.944 --> 00:00:52.362
After choosing, read the whole sentence to check it makes sense.

10
00:00:52.512 --> 00:00:56.706
Watch out! Because and so are easy to mix up!

11
00:00:56.856 --> 00:01:03.738
Being tired is the reason, going to bed early is the result. The reason comes first, so use so.

12
00:01:03.888 --> 00:01:09.570
We could also say: I went to bed early because I was tired.

13
00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:19.242
Your turn! I wanted to play, ___, it was raining. Which one? Pause and think.

14
00:01:19.392 --> 00:01:26.250
Wanting to play but it rains: opposite ideas, so but. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:36.042
Another one! Would you like rice, ___, noodles? Which one? Pause and think.

16
00:01:36.192 --> 00:01:41.178
It's a choice, so or. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:41.328 --> 00:01:51.498
Here's another! Ben was hungry, ___, he ate a sandwich. Which one? Pause and think.

18
00:01:51.648 --> 00:01:58.362
Being hungry is the reason, and it comes first, so so. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:58.512 --> 00:02:08.538
Try one more! We wore jackets, ___, it was cold. Which one? Pause and think.

20
00:02:08.688 --> 00:02:15.522
The cold is the reason, and it comes after, so because. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:15.672 --> 00:02:25.290
Try one more! My cat is black, ___, white. Which one? Pause and think.

22
00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:31.074
The cat has both colours, so and. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:31.224 --> 00:02:41.010
Try one more! You can walk, ___, take the bus. Which one? Pause and think.

24
00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:46.866
It's a choice between two, so or. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:47.016 --> 00:02:56.922
Last one! Mei smiled, ___, she won the race. Which one? Pause and think.

26
00:02:57.072 --> 00:03:03.282
Winning is the reason she smiled, so because. Did you get it right?

27
00:03:03.432 --> 00:03:13.770
Remember: and adds, but contrasts, or gives a choice, so gives a result, and because gives a reason. Think about how the ideas are linked, then choose.

28
00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:18.233
Use because to say why you like a food!

